{"sequence":14,"timestamp":"2026-03-29T19:52:23.324042419Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-6a5fe401","body":"In nitrogen_cycle.rs, after the comammox step (around line 350), `alk_budget` is not decremented by `comammox_alk_cost`, while `do_budget` IS always decremented after each step. Since nothing reads `alk_budget` after comammox this is harmless today, but if a future step (e.g. denitrification) needs the running alkalinity budget for rate-limiting, the stale value would silently over-allocate. Add `alk_budget = (alk_budget - comammox_alk_cost).max(0.0);` after line 350 to match the DO budget pattern and prevent a latent accounting bug.","dedup_key":"194c1b8f378ed91afa7fc5f8c4028aa861d35c844b86e5fd9ad0e0393124957f","run_id":"run-20260329191454","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":15,"timestamp":"2026-03-29T19:52:23.328086057Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-9ac12929","body":"In engine.rs, `StageTrace::metric()` unconditionally allocates `BudgetMetric` (including a heap `String` for the label) even when neither budget tracking nor tracing is enabled. For the nitrogen_cycle stage alone this is 5 allocations per tick, silently dropped if no budget ledger exists. Guard the allocation: either check `ctx.budget.is_some()` before calling `metric()`, or make `metric()` a no-op when a `budget_active` flag is false — similar to how `note()` already guards on `self.enabled`.","dedup_key":"c50605299c1ee8cd40ed1a2fc1119958ccad0b51228d50d28f2a8fd5817de3a3","run_id":"run-20260329191454","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
