{"sequence":28,"timestamp":"2026-03-29T20:16:20.063948270Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-f86e4833","body":"The `debug_assert` at nitrogen_cycle.rs:352-355 is vacuous: it checks `alk_budget <= state.water.alkalinity_meq_total + EPSILON`, but at that point `alk_budget` has been decremented (and clamped to ≥0) while `state.water.alkalinity_meq_total` has NOT yet been mutated (the actual pool deduction happens later at line 433-435). The condition `max(initial - costs, 0) <= initial + epsilon` is trivially true for any non-negative costs. Either replace with a meaningful check (e.g., assert that `aob_alk_cost + comammox_alk_cost <= state.water.alkalinity_meq_total + EPSILON` before the `.max(0.0)` clamp, which would catch an over-deduction) or remove it.","dedup_key":"ab3f51ae656371e5fd8c658e2eda5e093b0a8ef59fc2190952a4885fd6087ce3","run_id":"run-20260329191454","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
