{"sequence":41,"timestamp":"2026-03-29T20:38:42.378691929Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-3-bc178401","body":"In nitrogen_cycle.rs after the comammox budget deduction (around line 352), `alk_budget` is left stale at its pre-comammox value because the recent refactor replaced `alk_budget = (alk_budget - comammox_alk_cost).max(0.0)` with a local `let remaining_alk_budget`. Add `alk_budget = remaining_alk_budget.max(0.0);` after the debug_assert (or shadow `alk_budget` with `let alk_budget = ...`) to maintain the running-budget invariant. Without this, any future guild step added after comammox but before the final alkalinity commit at line 434 would silently read an inflated budget and over-allocate alkalinity.","dedup_key":"87299e11ba925f61495dd01939c8775e8210219a59d6ec33f44d755bf827d0f9","run_id":"run-20260329191454","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":42,"timestamp":"2026-03-29T20:38:42.387536775Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-3-67cf9ba0","body":"The constant MG_N_PER_MEQ_AMMONIA (= 14.007) is defined identically in both microfauna.rs:9 and shrimp.rs:9 for ammonia excretion alkalinity coupling. Centralize it in process.rs alongside NITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N and DENITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N, since all three derive from the atomic mass of nitrogen and govern alkalinity stoichiometry. This prevents future divergence if one copy is changed without the other.","dedup_key":"9bbf2c2f08d184507759d42c60ced8d530b49582af33dac103680f4da4eb8db2","run_id":"run-20260329191454","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
